      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_a07aecd779b4b45419310033feec73f00aca215ab2966d6f9989885e59d59553",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The method performs analytic transport rather than estimating the target line directly. Localization is purchased by kernel decay, while the tunable X mediates the tradeoff between the transported target integral and the contour error; the final proof is a self-consistent parameter balance.",
