    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_005d6e080e02b88c613cee3b416202f4a10d3d2f6aee8de130e3f5bf0d01dd15",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For both the second and fourth critical-line moments, the source localizes a global main-term-plus-error formula by differencing at the endpoints of a centered interval. The known global bound for E(T) is then lower order than the second-moment local main term when H=T^theta with theta>131/416, while the known bound for E_2(T) yields the fourth-moment local asymptotic at H=T^(2/3)log^C T. Thus the two sections support the same concrete mechanism: available error control sets a sufficient resolution threshold for recovering a local main term.",
