    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4fc9dcebbf85341e336fd184fdc4a2c53ab6b02ed1250729e27219e1bbc4c619",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "On the common regime of fixed integer k and fixed-power intervals H=T^theta, the source's unconditional lower bound and RH-conditional upper bound bracket the centered 2k-th critical-line moment by H times a logarithmic factor with exponent k^2, with the upper exponent carrying the stated O(1/log_3 T) loss. The bridge log H=theta log T for fixed theta makes the two formulas directly comparable.",
