    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ae15ccfb3dc2526e5773c7a4f891a6928828b7248bac7e2a96fb2353902295ff",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses distinct representation changes to make moment errors analytically accessible. For the second moment, Atkinson's dual oscillatory sums and the structurally different Riemann-Siegel double sums both represent E(T), opening exponential-sum or correlation estimates. For the fourth moment, Gaussian smoothing resolves convergence problems and permits a trace-formula passage to a spectral sum involving Maass data. Together these sections show a shared strategy of replacing a raw moment integral by a representation adapted to cancellation or convergence, without identifying the resulting objects.",
